    // WHY: this timer is a native watchdog for the generated renderer's normal
    // poll owner, not another poll loop. Terminal-frame scheduled/response
    // telemetry keeps it singleflight; a failed response backs off to 4s and an
    // unresolved request must remain stuck for a bounded 8s before fail-open.
    // This prevents the old 96ms timer from turning one 5s fetch into 53 request
    // opportunities while retaining foreground Working-tail recovery.
    private static final long CAPTURE_RENDERER_IDLE_REALTIME_REFRESH_BASE_MS = 2000;
    // WHY: FIX D (smoothness) — how long the local per-frame composite pump keeps
    // running after the last CHANGED accepted frame before auto-stopping (battery
    // safety). Must exceed CAPTURE_RENDERER_IDLE_REALTIME_REFRESH_BASE_MS (2000ms):
    // during active streaming the only native "new frame" signal is the 2s
    // idle-realtime poll, so a stop window <=2000ms would stall the pump between
    // polls mid-stream. 2600ms survives one poll + jitter yet still stops ~2.6s
    // after output goes idle. The 2s poll itself is unchanged (this is a local
    // compositor cadence, never a fetch cadence).
    private static final long CAPTURE_RENDERER_SMOOTHNESS_IDLE_STOP_MS = 2600L;
